<title>USA: Mercantile Bancorp ends Visa program.</title>
<headline>Mercantile Bancorp ends Visa program.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS, Mo. 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercantile Bancorporation Inc said Thursday it ended its co-branded credit card program with Southwestern Bell, a unit of SBC Communications Inc.</p>
<p>Mercantile said it is notifying the 500,000 current Southwestern Bell Visa cardholders the card will be replaced by its new MercRewards Visa card next month. The new card will maintain a two-percent cash reward feature, said the company.</p>
<p>Southwestern Bell Visa cards will remain valid until new cards are received or until the end of March, Mercantile said.</p>
<p>Mercantile is an $18.2-billion bank holding company.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
